# Install

There are no prebuilt releases yet, so both apps are built from source. Clone the repository first:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/kykurniawan/ligarview.git
cd ligarview
```

## The Mac app

Needs [Rust](https://rustup.rs) (stable) and Xcode's command line tools.

```bash
tools/bundle.sh
open host/target/Ligarview.app
```

`bundle.sh` builds the host and wraps it as `Ligarview.app` with an icon. Move it to **Applications** if you like. The first launch asks for **Screen Recording**: allow it in **System Settings → Privacy & Security → Screen & System Audio Recording**, then open the app again.

You can also run the host straight from a terminal, without the window:

```bash
cd host
cargo run --release
```

## The Android app

Needs the Android SDK and JDK 17 or newer. With the tablet connected and USB debugging on **just for this install**:

```bash
cd android
./gradlew installDebug
```

Or build the APK with `./gradlew assembleDebug` and copy `android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk` to the tablet any way you like. USB debugging is only needed to install; running Ligarview never needs it.

<p class="note">Next: <a href="/docs/connect">connect the tablet</a>.</p>
